preview when Bella wakes from an  afternoon slumber outside her village  she knows her short life will soon be  editin an ancient and powerful monster  mog chothra is coming and Bella will be  offered as a sacrifice of appeasement  this is a high honor both for Vella and  her family were very proud of you  elsewhere Shay rises for another mundane  day aboard the bossa nova a spaceship  designed to keep him safe and free from  harm the result is a child's paradise  turned prison as Shay can do little else  but eat ice cream play with toys and  receive hugs from his animatronic  friends together Bella and Shaco star  and broken age a coming-of-age story  that finds both heroes struggling to  break free of their stations in life you  can switch between these two freely and  help guide Vella and Shay as the  innocent worlds of their youth collapse  around them to reveal the often harsh  realities of adulthood it's a somber  tale but one that is tempered by the  colorful and humorous style that has  become developer Double Fine's hallmark  Bella decides against the warnings of  her family to fight mog chothra while  Shay devises a plan to outsmart the  overbearing spaceships and take control  of it for himself you accomplish both by  talking with others and collecting items  tasks which are punctuated with some  great humor that keeps you excited to  see what sorts of wacky scenarios the  game will throw at you next  whether you're hopping between head  shrieking teleporters or steering a  spaceship by way of knitting a scarf  broken age isn't afraid to juxtapose  it's more serious plot points with  ridiculous activities  however while delightfully silly both  Bella and Shea's worlds maintain a  consistent logic that helps you work out  these problems solving a puzzle is never  a matter of combining two wildly  different things to make some random  object related to the task at hand they  may be silly but these puzzles also make  sense however since the game is asking  you to juggle two entirely separate sets  of puzzles one for Bella and one for  Shay the puzzles themselves feel rather  basic and their solutions straight  forward the complexity of these puzzles  does ramp up slowly as you progress  further in the game but get cut short  when you reach broken ages early  conclusion presumably since this is only  the first half of a full game the  puzzles will continue to grow more  complex in the second act but this  remains to be seen when you're not  worrying about brain teasers broken ages  vibrant world is a delight to explore  the bright pastel colouring and soft  lighting Lin the game's backdrops a  storybook aesthetic that complements its  humorous writing while also contrasting  and emphasizing its central plotline at  times you feel as if you're dashing  through the pages of a dr. Seuss book  some fantastic voice work further  enhances this experience with a couple  of great performances by characters seen  only once or twice in the game broken  ages world may be fun to explore but  don't get too comfortable just as you  fall into a steady groove with its story  and its puzzles the game ends thankfully  the ending manages to provide some  resolution while also enticing you for a  second act it's obvious that while this  game functions as a standalone release  it's not designed to be one this opening  act has set the stage for an engrossing  tale of childhoods end let's just hope  the payoff is as fulfilling  you
 

